.TH APER 1 "July 26, 2026" "aper" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aper \- render Penrose tilings as PDF
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aper
.RB [ \-n " depth" ]
.br
.BR aper " " { \-h | \-\-help }
.br
.BR aper " " { \-V | \-\-version }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aper
generates a finite P3 Penrose tiling from a fixed ten-triangle sun seed
by Robinson subdivision and writes a complete native vector PDF to standard
output.
Diagnostics are written to standard error, so the PDF can be redirected or
piped without contamination.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-depth " " depth
Set the number of subdivisions to an integer from 1 through 12.
The default is 7.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a concise help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Render the default tiling and open it:
.PP
.EX
aper > tiling.pdf
open tiling.pdf
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B aper
exits zero after writing a complete PDF document and non-zero if its arguments
are invalid or output fails.
